  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">WWF: R&#xe4;dda naturen genom att st&#xe4;rka lokalsamh&#xe4;llen i Latin Amerika</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WWF: Saving nature, empowering people and improving livelihoods in Latin America</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen och framtida liknande insatser kommer att ge urfolk och lokalsamh&#xe4;llen, speciellt kvinnor och ungdomar, har tagit en central roll som st&#xe4;rkta innovat&#xf6;rer, genomf&#xf6;rare och f&#xf6;respr&#xe5;kare f&#xf6;r territoriell f&#xf6;rvaltning och klimat-l&#xf6;sningar som &#xe4;r till nytta f&#xf6;r b&#xe5;de folk och natur i prioriterade landskap i Latin-Amerika. Insatsen &#xe4;r ett projektst&#xf6;d som ber&#xf6;r milj&#xf6;-sociala fr&#xe5;gor som &#xe4;r viktiga i gr&#xe4;ns&#xf6;verskridande milj&#xf6;skydd (fr&#xe4;mst biogisk m&#xe5;ngfald och klimat) i Latin-Amerika. Den fokuserar p&#xe5; tre gr&#xe4;ns&#xf6;verskridande landskap i Latin-Amerika, d&#xe4;r WWF str&#xe4;var efter att involvera och st&#xe4;rka IPLC, g&#xf6;ra lokala r&#xf6;ster h&#xf6;rda samt driva p&#xe5; f&#xf6;r st&#xf6;rre j&#xe4;mlikhet inom IPLC  f&#xf6;r att vara aktiva och driva en h&#xe5;llbar utveckling till nytta f&#xf6;r folk och natur. Dessa landskap &#xe4;r hem f&#xf6;r urfolk och lokalsamh&#xe4;llen som har en viktig roll i h&#xe5;llbar utveckling men vars m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter ofta inte &#xe4;r respekterade eller genomf&#xf6;rda, inklusive deras r&#xe4;ttigheter till land, tillg&#xe5;ng till information och deltagande i beslutsprocesser. Ofta har dessa samh&#xe4;llen inte de f&#xf6;ruts&#xe4;ttningarna f&#xf6;r att g&#xf6;ra sina r&#xf6;ster h&#xf6;rda och att ha en framtr&#xe4;dande roll f&#xf6;r att p&#xe5;verka policyarbetet. Landskapen &#xe4;r utvalda f&#xf6;r att ge ett anv&#xe4;ndbart sammanhang f&#xf6;r j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhetsarbete f&#xf6;r  IPLC kvinnor &#xe4;r ofta uteslutna i beslutsprocesserna. Bristen p&#xe5; f&#xf6;rs&#xf6;rjningsm&#xf6;jligheter f&#xf6;r IPLC skapar ett stort tryck, framf&#xf6;r allt p&#xe5; kvinnor, som ofta l&#xe4;mnas i samh&#xe4;llena med barnen medan m&#xe4;nnen migrerar till st&#xe4;derna f&#xf6;r att s&#xf6;ka arbetstillf&#xe4;llen. Insatsen str&#xe4;var efter att genomf&#xf6;ra &#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder f&#xf6;r att minska dessa oj&#xe4;mlikheter och utmaningar.

Fr&#xe5;n regionalt och milj&#xf6;f&#xf6;rvaltningsperspektiv kommer fokuset p&#xe5; gr&#xe4;ns&#xf6;verskridande  landskap att ge ett merv&#xe4;rde eftersom detta m&#xf6;jligg&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra liknande ansatser och &#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder i varje land och att knyta samman skyddade omr&#xe5;den &#xf6;ver gr&#xe4;nserna. Genom att kombinera en landskaps-ansats med regional samordning kommer detta att leda till ett mer effektivt skydd av biologisk m&#xe5;ngfald till nytta f&#xf6;r m&#xe4;nniskor, som inte kan uppn&#xe5;s genom enbart nationella &#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder. Det kommer att bli m&#xf6;jligt att skala upp nyttan och p&#xe5;verkan genom delat l&#xe4;rande, bygga gr&#xe4;ns&#xf6;verskridande allianser f&#xf6;r att p&#xe5;verka policyarbete, och att arbeta med organisationer vars arbete sp&#xe4;nner &#xf6;ver gr&#xe4;nserna. 

Projektet arbetar med tre strategier: a) inkomstskapande aktiviteter som st&#xf6;der h&#xe5;llbar f&#xf6;rs&#xf6;rjning f&#xf6;r m&#xe4;n, kvinnor och deras familjer; b) kapacitets- och alliansbyggande f&#xf6;r r&#xe4;ttighetsb&#xe4;rande organisationer, och c) f&#xf6;rsvar f&#xf6;r j&#xe4;mlika klimat- och naturbaserade l&#xf6;sningar.  Insatsen bidrar till WWFs globala m&#xe5;l f&#xf6;r Skogsf&#xf6;rvaltning och de strategiska planerna f&#xf6;r WWF:s kontor involverade i denna insats &#xe4;r i linje med m&#xe5;len f&#xf6;r Strategin f&#xf6;r Sveriges regionala utvecklingssamarbete med Latin-Amerika 2021-2025.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The initiative and future like-minded interventions, will result in that indigenous peoples and local communities in particular women and youth, have claimed a central role as empowered innovators, implementers and advocates for territorial governance and climate solutions that benefit people and nature in priority landscapes in Latin America. The project is a project support and will address socio-environmental issues that are critical for transboundary nature protection (mainly biological diversity and climate) in Latin America.  It will focus on three key transboundary landscapes in Latin America, where WWF will aim to involve, empower, strengthen their voice, and pursue greater equity for IPLCs to be active in the pursuit of sustainable development that benefits people and nature.These landscapes are home to indigenous and local communities, who can play a key role in sustainable development, but whose human rights are often not adequately respected or implemented, including their right to land, access to information and participation in decision making processes.  These communities often do not have the necessary prerequisites to amplify their voices and have a more prominent role in policy influencing. The landscapes selected also provide a useful context for addressing gender equality because IPLC women are often excluded for decision making processes.  The lack of economic opportunities for IPLCs in these places particular pressure on women who are often left in the community with children when men migrate to the city in search of employment.  The project aims to implement measures to address these inequality and challenges.  

From a regional and environmental management perspective, the focus on these transboundary landscapes will add value because it makes it possible to implement similar approaches and actions in each country and address connectivity needs between protected areas and across borders. Combining a landscape approach and regional coordination will lead to more effective conservation of biodiversity and benefits for people, which cannot be achieved through purely national interventions.  It will be possible to scale up impacts through shared learning, building alliances across borders for policy influencing and work with organizations that transcend national borders

Three main strategies will orient the course of this project:  a) income-generating activities that promote sustainable livelihoods for men, women and their families, b) building capacities and alliances of rightsholders&#x2019; organizations, and c) advocacy for equitable climate and nature solutions.  This project contributes to WWF global goals for Forest and Governance, the strategic plans of the WWF offices involved in this proposal and is aligned with the objectives in the strategy for Sweden&#x2019;s regional development cooperation with Latin America 2021&#x2013;2025.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project has three main outcomes with associated short- , medium, and long -term objectives: 

1. Income generating activities that promote sustainable livelihoods, human wellbeing , and natural resource management

 - By 2024, at least 15 income generating activities are prioritized with rightholders.

 - By 2025, at least 8 income generating activities are being implemented  with adaptive management considerations.

 - By 2026, At least 5,000 IPLC people participating in income generating activities.

2.  Building capacities and alliances of rightsholders for more empowered territorial governance

 - By 2023, at least 15 IPLC organizations (5 per landscape) trained in organizationaland financial management and territorial governance.

 - By 2024, at least 30  IPLC will be trained on advocacy and leadership.

 - By 2025, at least 6 alliances (2 per landscape) between IPLCs and other key stakeholders  should be established to support equittable climate and nature solutions

3.  IPLCs have a stronger voice for equittable climate and nature solutions

 - By 2025  at least 15 IPLC organizations have amplified their voices in public debate for equitable climate and nature solutions</narrative>
  </description>
